# qualification's route as the lead page's Re-score sends it (core/modules/qualification/README.md
# "Screen", "The re-score"): one person, answered 202 with the request's id and `marked`, the leads the
# worker's run moves with the saved criteria: 0 when the criteria that scored the lead are the saved
# ones, or when it has no scored snapshot at the ICP's version. The snapshot the page then asks for
# is alpha-p6-060-lead-page.http's; every scored lead at once, alpha-p6-040-rescore.http's.
# A write sends the cookie, so it sends Origin: {{appOrigin}} too. `personId` is a person of your
# workspace with a lead: put it in http-client.private.env.json.

### POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/qualification/rescore: the lead page's Re-score of one person
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/qualification/rescore
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
Idempotency-Key: 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000100

{ "personIds": ["{{personId}}"] }
